				<div class="dp-box-content">
					<p>Moving an existing DeskPRO installation to a new server is fairly straightforward. Here are the steps you should follow:</p>
					<ol>
						<li>Generate a dump of your MySQL database and restore it on your new server.</li>
						<li>Copy all of the DeskPRO files from your old server to your new server.</li>
						<li>Edit /includes/config.php and update the database details.</li>

						<li>Make sure the /datastore/ directory (and it's contents) is still writable (for example, CHMOD it to 0777).</li>
						<li>If you have moved your entire domain to the new server, make sure any configured POP3 accounts are set up properly. If you are using the PIPE'ing mechanism, make sure you reconfigure your new mail server.</li>
						<li>Reconfigure the required scheduled tasks.</li>
						<li>If you have moved to a brand new domain name, make sure to update the <i>Helpdesk URL</i> setting in the DeskPRO Admin CP.</li>
					</ol>
					<p>Note: We also offer a relocation service that you can purchase from the <a href="http://members.deskpro.com/">members area</a>.</p>

